# FDD 22 review — "22 - Data Collection & Compliance - Employee Assignment Details"
# (Features 22.1-22.5), plus Feature 22.6 (Appropriate Placement Audit) from the companion
# folder document "21.7; 22.6 - ... Employee and Appropriate Placement Audit.docx".
#
# Ingested per abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md against the mied-v3 Staffing graph
# (staffing-domain.ttl / staffing-permissions.ttl / staffing-api.ttl / staffing-sequences.ttl /
# staffing-technical-design.ttl, all loaded together), with cred:Op_GetEducatorCredentials and
# comm:CommunicationsContext referenced as already-real cross-domain IRIs (both declared in
# credentialing-domain.ttl / communications' own files, not redeclared here).
#
# *** RESOLUTION OF THE FDD-29-FLAGGED GAP (see this repo's GAPS.md, FDD 29 section) ***
# GAPS.md currently states, from the FDD 29 pass: "Data Collection & Compliance — Employee
# Assignment Details (22) — referenced as supplying data consumed by credential application
# workflows; no corresponding domain conversion exists (22 is one of several Data Collection
# & Compliance FDD folders with no mapped bounded context at all)." Having now actually read
# FDD 22 in full against staffing-domain.ttl (a real, converted CoreDomain, not a stub): THIS
# CLAIM IS NO LONGER (AND WAS ARGUABLY NEVER) ACCURATE. staff:AssignmentAggregate is
# essentially a direct model of this FDD's own subject matter (Assignment Details, Education
# Job Type-driven data-element requirements, Credential Error Justification, endorsement/SCED
# validation) down to near-verbatim invariant wording (see Req_22_3_2 below, a citation-verified
# word-for-word match). staff:EmployeeRosterAggregate's EducationHistory/EvaluationOutcome/
# NewTeacherMonitoring sub-entities, staff:CollectionAggregate (certification workflow), and
# staff:AuditWorkItemAggregate (the Appropriate Placement Audit half, Feature 22.6) round out
# the rest of this FDD's scope. The likely explanation: FDD 29's own pass was scoped to
# Credentialing and treated FDD 22 as an un-reviewed dependency without cross-checking whether
# a domain conversion existed elsewhere in the batch under a name FDD 29 wasn't looking for
# ("staffing" rather than "Data Collection & Compliance") — an easy miss when reviewing one
# domain's Dependencies section in isolation. This pass's own finding, to replace that GAPS.md
# entry with: FDD 22 IS covered by the real, converted staffing bounded context; remaining gaps
# are narrow and API-surface-specific (see below and staffing-permissions.ttl's own header),
# not "no corresponding domain conversion at all."
#
# Structure of the source material and what's used as the Requirement unit:
# - "22 - Collection & Compliance - Employee Assignment Details.docx" has a long Business
#   Specifications prose section (the real design detail) and a 97-row "HIGH LEVEL SCENARIOS"
#   paraphrase table restating the same content at coarser grain — the HLS table is skipped per
#   CONVENTIONS.md. Its own Addendum gives real Feature/story numbering: 22.1.1-22.1.7
#   (Instructional Staff), 22.2.1-22.2.3 (Non-Instructional Staff), 22.3.1-22.3.3 (Student
#   Support Staff), 22.4 (Data Input via API/File Upload — one paragraph, no numbered stories
#   of its own, explicitly pointing at FDD 21.5's stories instead), 22.5 (Email/Comm — one
#   paragraph, no numbered stories, pointing at Business Specifications #6 and #4). These two
#   pointer "features" are modeled below as single plain sd:Requirement nodes (Req_22_4,
#   Req_22_5), not sd:UserStory, since neither is phrased as a story nor carries its own
#   acceptance criteria — each gets an out-of-scope Annotation rather than false story content.
# - The companion folder document "21.7; 22.6 - ... Employee and Appropriate Placement
#   Audit.docx" covers TWO FDDs at once (per CONVENTIONS.md's "Cross-document FDD groups"
#   guidance): Feature 21.7 (Employee Audit, an FDD-21 concern) and Feature 22.6 (Appropriate
#   Placement Audit, an FDD-22 concern). Per this session's brief, FDD 21 is being reviewed
#   concurrently by another agent — so ONLY Feature 22.6's five stories (22.6.1-22.6.5) are
#   modeled below; Feature 21.7's three stories (21.7.1-21.7.3) are deliberately NOT modeled
#   here and are left for FDD 21's own review pass to pick up.
# - Business Specifications-section-only content that never got its own Addendum story number
#   (e.g. the Collection Exception e-form's district/DQ-issue/records-impacted field detail
#   from comment 373610033, or the bulk-file-upload workflow) is folded into notes on the
#   closest related story rather than promoted to a synthetic Requirement of its own — the
#   Addendum's own numbering is treated as authoritative for what counts as a distinct item,
#   consistent with FDD 29's precedent of only using synthetic IDs when a real, wireframed,
#   field-level capability was entirely missing from the numbering (not the case here).
#
# Comments (16 across both docx files, read via comments.xml): most are short, resolved
# one-off wording clarifications (exception vs. exemption terminology; "add examples";
# duplicate-field flags) folded into notes on the nearest story rather than modeled
# individually. Three comments surfaced substantive findings, modeled as Annotations below:
# a credential/endorsement-to-position mapping OWNERSHIP ambiguity (comment 12: "Maybe MiEd
# admin? MOECS also collects this info, this is reviewed as part of credential apps" — raised
# against the Dependencies section's flat claim that "MiEdWorkforce Admin (12.1)" owns this),
# a New-Teacher-Mentor search-alignment note (comment 16) that independently corroborates
# staffing-domain.ttl's own existing staff:Question_MentorVerificationEndpointDirection (not
# re-raised as a new Annotation, just cross-referenced), and a bulk-upload file-format question
# (comment 1124016608, "Can the users upload an excel file?") that independently corroborates
# staffing-permissions.ttl's own documented staffing.employee-roster.bulk-upload API-surface
# gap (also not re-raised, just cross-referenced).
#
# Wireframes: neither docx captions its images "Wireframe N" (unlike FDD 29/11/16's pattern).
# The main FDD's 6 images (word/media/image1-6.png) are a mix of legacy "MORE"-system
# screenshots (Education History display/entry, Evaluation Outcome update — images 1-5) and one
# modern MiEdWorkforce mockup (a generic file-upload screen, image6, captioned nowhere in text —
# its File Type dropdown reads "Identity", and its supported formats are .doc/.docx/.pdf, which
# does NOT match the Business Specifications' own claim that bulk Employee Roster uploads
# support Excel/CSV/XML — flagged as a discrepancy below since these may be two different upload
# surfaces the FDD conflates, or a genuine format mismatch). All 6 were viewed; images 3-5 are
# near-duplicate steps of the same Evaluation Outcome update flow (only image3 extracted in
# full, images 4-5 confirmed as the same screen advancing through save states — not
# individually described further, per depth-calibration guidance). The companion document's 7
# images (media/image.png, image2-7.png — note the irregular "image.png" with no numeral,
# matching FDD 29's own observation of packaging quirks in these documents) are modern,
# higher-fidelity MiEdWorkforce mockups; 5 of 7 were viewed and extracted (image6 was not
# individually viewed — confirmed structurally identical to image.png/image4.png's worklist
# pattern by its thumbnail, not a distinct screen). All extracted to wireframes/ below.
#
# Depth calibration: 18 real numbered stories (13 from the main FDD, 5 from the companion's
# Feature 22.6) plus 2 pointer-feature Requirements — a mid-sized FDD, reviewed at full
# per-story depth (no batching of near-identical stories was needed; the closest case,
# 22.2.1/22.3.1's near-identical "specific Local Job Function required" language, is still
# modeled as two distinct stories since each targets a different Education Job Type).

@prefix sd:    <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:> .
@prefix oa:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix staff: <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:> .
@prefix cred:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:> .
@prefix comm:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:> .

#################################################################
# Source documents
#################################################################

