    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: 'Employee Information' side-drawer (Name, Certificate #, Certificate Type, National Board Certified, Renewal Status), an Endorsements table (Subject/Grade, Institution, Nullified), a Certificate History table (App#/Iss. Date/Exp. Date/Status, two rows both Expired), an Assignments table (same App#/date/status column shape — appears to reuse the Certificate History row shape rather than showing actual staffing assignment data, possibly a mockup placeholder issue rather than intentional), a Remarks table (Comment/Created by/Date Created) with an 'Add Comment' action, and a highlighted red 'Add to Investigation' panel/button. Corroborates Req_22_6_3's acceptance criteria field list closely, but ALSO shows an 'Add to Investigation' capability with no backing narrative anywhere in either document's numbered stories or Business Specifications prose — an undocumented UI affordance, not raised as its own Annotation given it's a single unexplained button, but noted for visibility." ;
